      "id": "P1",
      "text": "COLONOSCOPY REPORT"
    },
    {
      "id": "P2",
      "text": "Date of service: November 9, 2026"
    },
    {
      "id": "P3",
      "text": "Endoscopist: Naomi Carrow, MD (fictional)"
    },
    {
      "id": "P4",
      "text": "Procedure: The colonoscope was advanced to the cecum; the appendiceal orifice was identified."
    },
    {
      "id": "P5",
      "text": "- Mid transverse colon: a 30 mm flat, granular laterally spreading lesion."
    },
    {
      "id": "P6",
      "text": "- The lesion was not removed today because clopidogrel had not been held."
    },
    {
      "id": "P7",
      "text": "- Today a submucosal tattoo was placed 3 cm distal to the lesion for future localization."
    },
    {
      "id": "P8",
      "text": "- The tattoo used sterile carbon particle suspension injected in three quadrants."
    },
    {
      "id": "P9",
      "text": "1. 30 mm laterally spreading lesion of the transverse colon, tattooed today; not resected."
    },
    {
      "id": "P10",
      "text": "Plan: Endoscopic mucosal resection at a separate session after clopidogrel is held."
    }
  ],
